# Test JOIN-RANGE-11: two-sided bounded range on the right (inner)
# table's indexed column. The trickier case for SideAccess.cmp2 -- the
# inner range must be re-seeked and independently bounded-checked for
# *every* outer row, and a bound failure must only end that one outer
# row's inner walk (routing to addr_done_inner), not abort the whole
# query the way the same failure on the outer side does. Engineering
# (budget 500) is correctly excluded from every course that joins to
# it, while Math (200) and Physics (300) still come through for the
# courses that join to them.

USE join-range-fixture.cdb

%%

SELECT title, name, budget FROM courses NATURAL JOIN departments WHERE departments.budget > 100 AND departments.budget < 400;

%%

"Calculus"           "Math"     200
"Advanced Calculus"  "Math"     200
"Thermodynamics"     "Physics"  300
